It comforts me that you got confused by this code as well. Holy moly.
`resetWaitEvent` used to be an out parameter of the `_ReadBuffer` function, which had only 1 caller: this function (`Read`). `resetWaitEvent` was set like this by `_ReadBuffer`:
```cpp
resetWaitEvent = true;

// ...

// signal if we emptied the buffer
if (_storage.empty())
{
    resetWaitEvent = true;
}
```

`Read` in turn did this:
```cpp
if (resetWaitEvent)
{
    ServiceLocator::LocateGlobals().hInputEvent.ResetEvent();
}
```

By merging `_ReadBuffer` into `Read` the `resetWaitEvent` is gone and got replaced with `_storage.empty()`.

I'm not quite seeing what you mean, when looking at the current code: https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/blob/814e44bf45762ee878b41553c7048c6ffbf1e63e/src/host/readDataCooked.cpp#L1116-L1123

If you remove all the unrelated code and simplify it a bit you arrive at:
```cpp
DWORD LineCount = 1;

if (_echoInput)
{
    ProcessAliases(LineCount);
}

// `_bytesRead > _userBufferSize` is true when there's more data than the user requested.
if (_bytesRead > _userBufferSize || LineCount > 1)
{
    if (LineCount > 1)
    {
        pInputReadHandleData->SaveMultilinePendingInput(pending);
    }
    else
    {
        pInputReadHandleData->SavePendingInput(pending);
    }
}
else
{
}
```

